  "id": "876619727",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "So-called West Church in Apollonia",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/basilica",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/architecturalcomplex"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The site was already mentioned in a 1828 survey, but was excavated only in 1958-9. The many irregularities in the layout suggest the continuous re-use and adaptation of previous architectural elements, from Roman to Late Antique times.\u00a0</p>",
